  "title": "\"Just last year, almost 400,000 people from Sudan have moved to South...",
  "description": "\"Just last year, almost 400,000 people from Sudan have moved to South Sudan and are climate refugees essentially because of floods. That is the level of actual climate impact we are seeing on displacement.\" Amitabh Behar, Executive Director, Oxfam International  Disasters, the adverse effects of climate change, and environmental degradation increasingly affect the livelihoods, resilience, and human rights of people around the world. These challenges compel people to leave their homes and countries of origin or trap them in areas at risk and in situations of high vulnerability. Increased international action and cooperation are critical to minimize the adverse drivers of human mobility, assist and protect those displaced and on the move, and ensure dignified and sustainable long-term solutions for affected populations.  #COP29",
